= Using the iconvert class =

The [../classes/html/classiconvert.html iconvert class] implements a character encoding converter.

It can be used to convert strings between various character encodings, such as between char, wchar_t, and UCS-2, or between any encodings supported by the system's iconv implementation.

To convert between encodings, create an instance of iconvert, set the from and to encodings, set the from and to buffers and their sizes, and call convert().

The "from encoding" and "to encoding" use standard iconv encoding names.  An empty string for the encoding indicates the default system encoding.  "WCHAR_T" indicates the wchar_t encoding.  "UCS-2BE" and "UCS-2LE" indicate big-endian and little-endian UCS-2 encodings.

